// ERD for the Cucumber Studio-like BDD platform.
// Owner: pm proposes, backend-swe keeps the as-built part in sync with the JPA entities.
// Legend: blue headers = as-built (auth-service code), orange headers = proposed (approved design 2026-10-12, not yet implemented).
// View: paste into https://dbdiagram.io or open with a DBML plugin. See docs/erd/README.md.

Project cucumber {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
  **As-built at 2026-10-12** (branch staging, HEAD 32eee07 plus the uncommitted auth-service phase 1 work, Batches A–C, review point C; no file under model/ was modified, and the Hibernate DDL was checked against this file). backend-swe keeps this in sync.

  **Conventions (all services)**
  - Primary keys: `id uuid`. auth-service generates them in the application (`@GeneratedValue(strategy = AUTO)` on a UUID field).
  - Names: snake_case tables and columns. Hibernate default naming turns camelCase fields into snake_case, so `seatLimit` becomes `seat_limit`.
  - Timestamps: `created_at` on every table, and `updated_at` on every mutable table. Immutable rows (history, attachments) have only `created_at`. As-built auth-service uses `LocalDateTime`, which maps to `timestamp(6)` without a zone. Proposed tables use `timestamptz` in UTC, matching the planned move to Instant (auth-service phase 4).
  - Enums are stored as strings (`@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)`) and modelled as DBML Enums. Values are UPPER_SNAKE_CASE like the Java constants. An API may present execution statuses in lower case (passed, failed, ...), which is a contract decision, not a storage one.
  - Each service owns its own database. **There are no cross-service foreign keys.** A column that points into another service is a plain uuid with a note "references <service>.<table>.id (by ID, no FK)".
  - Within one service, relations are real foreign keys (Ref).

  **Legend**
  - Table note starts with "as-built": the table exists today exactly as described.
  - Table note starts with "proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented": a domain design by pm, approved by the user on 2026-10-12 (ERD-D1..D11). Nothing is built yet.
  - "proposed (auth-service phase 1)" would mark an entity change planned by docs/specs/auth-service.md but not yet in code. **Phase 1 plans none**: its "Will not be touched" list includes every entity in model/. Phase 1 only changes the values written (lower-cased emails, plan FREE, seat_limit 5), and those are noted on the columns.
  - "proposed (auth-service-projects)" marked the entity changes of docs/specs/auth-service-projects.md (E31, E36, E37) and its project rules. All of them are implemented (Batches A2, B and C, 2026-10-13), so no auth_service line carries the marker any more.
  - "proposed (auth-service-persistence)" marks a change of the auth_service group planned by docs/specs/auth-service-persistence.md (Ready, approved by the user 2026-10-14): PostgreSQL 17 with Flyway, timestamptz/Instant, NOT NULL and lengths, enums as varchar(32) plus a named CHECK (the DBML Enums above stay until then, because the H2 columns are native enums), lower-case email checks, a unique (org_id, lower(name)) index on projects, foreign-key indexes, named foreign keys with ON DELETE RESTRICT, and audit_log dropped. As-built lines are kept, with a note saying what will change. backend-swe updates each line and drops the marker when its E-item lands (spec T3 to T10).
  - "proposed (scenario-service)" marks a refinement of the scenario_service design by docs/specs/scenario-service.md (Ready, approved by the user on 2026-10-14). It applies on top of the 2026-10-12 design: jsonb instead of json, names as text, path uniqueness among active features only, tag_assignments.feature_id, enums stored as varchar(32) plus CHECK (ERD-D12), named constraints and delete rules per the database pattern (spec D14), and the id-stability and content rules (spec D8 to D12). The DBML Enums of scenario_service stay for readability; the real columns are varchar(32) with a CHECK, as noted on each column. backend-swe turns the scenario_service tables into as-built when its Flyway V1 migration and entities land (spec T2, T7).

  **Runtime database today:** H2 in-memory, schema generated by Hibernate (`ddl-auto: create`). There are no migrations. PostgreSQL plus Flyway is auth-service phase 4. Type notes below say where H2 and PostgreSQL DDL differ.
  proposed (auth-service-persistence): auth-service moves to PostgreSQL 17, database auth_service (UTF-8, locale provider builtin, C.UTF-8), schema from Flyway migrations V1 (the current entities exactly) to V7, ddl-auto validate. flyway_schema_history is managed by Flyway and not modelled here. Shared conventions for all services: spec section "Database pattern for every service".
  scenario-service starts directly on PostgreSQL 17 (database scenario_service, builtin C.UTF-8) with Flyway migrations and `ddl-auto: validate`, following the same "Database pattern for every service" (docs/specs/scenario-service.md D14); it never uses H2.
  '''
}

// =====================================================================
// AS-BUILT: auth-service (com.example.authservice.model, enums)
// =====================================================================

Enum user_status {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  PENDING_VERIFICATION [note: 'set by register and by anonymous invitation acceptance. Phase 1 (D4): may log in; only SUSPENDED is blocked.']
}

Enum plan {
  FREE [note: 'set by createOrganization; the only plan written in phase 1']
  TEAM
  ENTERPRISE
}

Enum organization_role {
  OWNER [note: 'rank 4 (rank is Java-only via isAtLeast, not stored)']
  ADMIN [note: 'rank 3']
  MEMBER [note: 'rank 2']
  READER [note: 'rank 1']
}

Enum project_role {
  ADMIN [note: 'rank 4 (rank is Java-only via isAtLeast, not stored)']
  MEMBER [note: 'rank 3']
  TESTER [note: 'rank 2']
  READER [note: 'rank 1']
}

Enum invitation_status {
  PENDING
  ACCEPTED
  REVOKED
  EXPIRED [note: 'never written by code today; expiry is computed from expires_at, so a stored PENDING may already be expired (spec glossary)']
}

Table users [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  email varchar(255) [unique, not null, note: 'unique is case-sensitive in the DB. The application trims and lower-cases emails before storing and comparing them (D12), and the API limits them to 254 characters (E17). proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(254), unique uk_users_email kept, plus CHECK ck_users_email_lower_case (email = lower(email)) (E70, E72).']
  password_hash varchar(255) [null, note: 'explicitly nullable (@Column(nullable = true)); BCrypt hash. proposed (auth-service-persistence): unchanged, stays nullable (D8).']
  full_name varchar(255) [null, note: 'no @Column: nullable, default length 255. The API limits it to 100 characters (E17). proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(100) not null; no control characters, lone surrogates or Unicode-blank values (E70, D11).']
  status user_status [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable. H2 DDL: native enum(...); PostgreSQL DDL: varchar(255) plus a check constraint. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_users_status_values (E70, E71).']
  mfa_enabled boolean [not null, note: 'primitive boolean, so Hibernate adds NOT NULL; no DB default']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'set by application code, no @CreationTimestamp. proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null, set from the service clock (E69, E70).']
  updated_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'set once at register; nothing updates it later. proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']

  Note: 'as-built (entity User, @Table users)'
}

Table organizations [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  name varchar(255) [null, note: 'no @Column: nullable, length 255 in the DB. The API limits it to 1-100 non-blank characters (E17); duplicates are allowed. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(100) not null, stored as sent (E70).']
  plan plan [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_organizations_plan_values (E70, E71).']
  seat_limit int [null, note: 'Integer; null means unlimited (spec glossary). createOrganization sets app.orgs.free-seat-limit (default 5). Seats used = members + PENDING invitations not yet expired (D11). proposed (auth-service-persistence): CHECK ck_organizations_seat_limit_positive (seat_limit IS NULL OR seat_limit > 0) (E70).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']

  Note: 'as-built (entity Organization, @Table organizations). No updated_at column. Invitations, acceptances, role changes and removals lock this row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) so the seat limit and the last-owner rule hold under concurrent requests.'
}

Table org_memberships [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  org_id uuid [not null]
  role organization_role [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable in the DB although every membership needs a role. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_org_memberships_role_values (E70, E71).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']

  indexes {
    (user_id, org_id) [unique, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): named uk_org_memberships_user_id_org_id']
    org_id [name: 'ix_org_memberships_org_id', note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): foreign-key index (E73)']
  }
  Note: 'as-built (entity OrgMembership). Exactly one role per user and organization. created_at is joinedAt in the member list. Rows are deleted when a member is removed or leaves.'
}

Table projects [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  org_id uuid [not null]
  name varchar(255) [null, note: 'nullable, no uniqueness in the DB. The API (T11) limits it to 1-100 non-blank characters as sent (counted before trimming), stores it trimmed, and keeps it unique per organization (trimmed, lower-cased with Locale.ROOT, archived projects included) in the application, under the organization row lock. A DB unique index on (org_id, lower(name)) and NOT NULL come with phase 4. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(100) not null (E70) and the unique index uk_projects_org_id_name_lower (E72).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']
  archived_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'set when the project is archived, null when active (E31, D5). Archived projects stay readable but are read-only; there is no hard delete. Becomes timestamptz in phase 4. proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz, null (E69).']

  indexes {
    (org_id, `lower(name)`) [unique, name: 'uk_projects_org_id_name_lower', note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): archived projects included (E72). The application check under the organization lock stays the primary rule (PROJECT_NAME_TAKEN). Also serves as the index for the org_id foreign key.']
  }

  Note: '''
  as-built (entity Project, Lombok accessors and builder, E31). secret_token was removed (E31, D8): the CI upload token for automated result ingestion (ERD-D2) comes with the result-ingestion spec, hashed with SHA-256, shown once, several per project, revocable, likely as its own table.
  Other services reference projects.id by ID and check access through GET /internal/projects/{projectId}/access (contract C5, ERD-D1; built in auth-service-projects T7).
  Project API under /api/orgs/{orgId}/projects (T11, T12): create, list, view, rename, archive and restore. No hard delete. Every write takes the organization row lock (P13).
  '''
}

Table project_memberships [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  project_id uuid [not null]
  role project_role [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_project_memberships_role_values (E70, E71).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']

  indexes {
    (user_id, project_id) [unique, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): named uk_project_memberships_user_id_project_id']
    project_id [name: 'ix_project_memberships_project_id', note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): foreign-key index (E73)']
  }
  Note: '''
  as-built (entity ProjectMembership). Read by the effective-role resolver (ProjectRoleService, D3): organization OWNER and ADMIN are implicit project ADMIN without a row, and an organization READER row counts as at most READER.
  Written by the project member API (T13, T14) and by organization changes (T15). Rules, enforced in the application: a row exists only for a current member of the project organization; an organization READER row holds at most READER. Leaving or being removed from the organization deletes the user rows in that organization projects (E38), and a demotion to organization READER lowers higher roles to READER (E39), in the same transaction. Writes take the organization row lock.
  '''
}

Table invitations [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  email varchar(255) [null, note: 'nullable, case-sensitive in the DB. The application trims and lower-cases it (D12). proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(254) not null, CHECK ck_invitations_email_lower_case (E70, E72).']
  org_id uuid [not null, note: 'required (join column nullable = false, E36): invitations are for organizations only (D7).']
  role organization_role [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable (E37, D7): an organization role only; stored values (OWNER, ADMIN, MEMBER, READER) are unchanged. On H2 an ENUM column; the PostgreSQL check or enum type comes with phase 4. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_invitations_role_values (E70, E71).']
  invited_by uuid [not null]
  token varchar(255) [unique, null, note: 'unique but nullable; acceptance token (24 random bytes, 32 URL-safe characters), stored in plain text. Returned once, in the create-invitation response. proposed (auth-service-persistence): not null, unique uk_invitations_token (E70).']
  status invitation_status [null, note: 'EnumType.STRING, nullable. Written: PENDING on create, ACCEPTED on accept, REVOKED on revoke. proposed (auth-service-persistence): varchar(32) not null, CHECK ck_invitations_status_values (E70, E71).']
  expires_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'created_at + 7 days, set by the application. proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null, from the service clock (E69, E70).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null, note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): timestamptz not null (E69, E70).']

  indexes {
    (org_id, email) [name: 'ix_invitations_org_id_email', note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): foreign-key index for org_id, also used by the pending-invitation lookups (E73)']
    invited_by [name: 'ix_invitations_invited_by', note: 'proposed (auth-service-persistence): foreign-key index (E73)']
  }

  Note: '''
  as-built (entity Invitation). Organization-only since E36 (D7): the project_id column, its foreign key and the project branch of the accept flow were removed. There are no project invitations; project members are added directly from the organization (D6).
  "One pending, unexpired invitation per organization and email" (D11) is enforced only in the application, not by a DB constraint. proposed (auth-service-persistence): it stays application-only, because "pending" depends on expires_at > now(), which a partial index can't express (spec D8 item 7).
  Accepting locks the row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) before any user or membership is written, so a token is single use (Q5).
  '''
}

Table audit_log [headercolor: #2D6A9F] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  actor_id uuid [not null]
  action varchar(255) [null, note: 'free text, no enum of actions']
  org_id uuid [null]
  project_id uuid [null]
  target_user_id uuid [null]
  metadata json [null, note: 'String field with columnDefinition json. Risk: PostgreSQL rejects a varchar bound to a json column without a cast or @JdbcTypeCode(SqlTypes.JSON), and H2 stores it as a JSON string literal (double-encoded).']
  created_at timestamp(6) [null]

  Note: 'as-built (entity AuditLog, @Table audit_log, singular unlike the other tables). No accessors and no writer. Audit writing was deferred to phase 2 (phase-1 D8); docs/specs/auth-service-projects.md D11 proposes deferring it again, to its own spec auth-service-audit, which must first fix the metadata mapping. proposed (auth-service-persistence): this table, its four foreign keys, the entity and AuditLogRepository are dropped by V7 (E74, option B, approved 2026-10-14). auth-service-audit creates audit_logs (plural) with metadata jsonb in its own migration.'
}

// proposed (auth-service-persistence): every auth_service foreign key is recreated as fk_<table>_<column> with ON DELETE RESTRICT (E73, spec D8 item 9).
// The [delete: restrict] marks are added when V6 lands; the audit_log Refs go with the table (E74).
Ref: org_memberships.user_id > users.id
Ref: org_memberships.org_id > organizations.id
Ref: projects.org_id > organizations.id
Ref: project_memberships.user_id > users.id
Ref: project_memberships.project_id > projects.id
Ref: invitations.org_id > organizations.id
Ref: invitations.invited_by > users.id
Ref: audit_log.actor_id > users.id // proposed (auth-service-persistence): dropped with audit_log (E74)
Ref: audit_log.org_id > organizations.id // proposed (auth-service-persistence): dropped with audit_log (E74)
Ref: audit_log.project_id > projects.id // proposed (auth-service-persistence): dropped with audit_log (E74)
Ref: audit_log.target_user_id > users.id // proposed (auth-service-persistence): dropped with audit_log (E74)

TableGroup auth_service {
  users
  organizations
  org_memberships
  projects
  project_memberships
  invitations
  audit_log
}

// =====================================================================
// PROPOSED: scenario-service (Gherkin content)
// Refinements marked "proposed (scenario-service)" come from docs/specs/scenario-service.md (Ready, approved 2026-10-14).
// Storage per ERD-D12: every enum column below is varchar(32) + CHECK ck_<table>_<column>_values, not a PostgreSQL ENUM type.
// =====================================================================

Enum scenario_kind {
  BACKGROUND [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum). Background steps are not a test case on their own.']
  SCENARIO [note: 'Scenario or Example keyword']
  SCENARIO_OUTLINE [note: 'Scenario Outline or Scenario Template keyword; has examples']
}

Enum step_keyword {
  GIVEN [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum)']
  WHEN
  THEN
  AND
  BUT
  ASTERISK [note: 'the * bullet keyword']
}

Enum step_argument_type {
  NONE [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum)']
  DATA_TABLE
  DOC_STRING
}

Enum tag_target_type {
  FEATURE [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum)']
  RULE
  SCENARIO [note: 'also used for Scenario Outline']
  EXAMPLES
}

Table features [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  path varchar(1024) [not null, note: 'path of the .feature file in the project, e.g. features/checkout/payment.feature. Replaces a folder table in the MVP. proposed (scenario-service): stored as sent; relative POSIX path ending in .feature, no leading /, no empty, . or .. segment, no backslash or control character (spec D10). Can change on a save; a path change alone creates no version.']
  name text [not null, note: 'text after Feature: in the current version. proposed (scenario-service): text instead of varchar(500), and may be empty (Cucumber accepts "Feature:" without a name).']
  description text [not null, note: 'as the parser reports it (leading indentation kept). proposed (scenario-service): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7).']
  language varchar(10) [not null, default: 'en', note: 'from the Gherkin # language: header. The longest dialect code must fit (spec A10).']
  current_version int [not null, note: 'feature_versions.version that the parsed tables (rules, scenarios, steps, examples) reflect']
  created_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  updated_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  archived_at timestamptz [null, note: 'soft delete: results in report_service keep pointing at this id. proposed (scenario-service): archived features are read-only, hidden from default lists and the tag catalogue, and free their path; restore clears this (spec D11).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, `lower(path)`) [unique, name: 'uk_features_project_id_path_lower', note: 'proposed (scenario-service): replaces the plain unique (project_id, path); its leading project_id also serves the feature list. In PostgreSQL it is a PARTIAL unique index: UNIQUE (project_id, lower(path)) WHERE archived_at IS NULL. DBML cannot express the WHERE clause, so SQL generated from this file is stricter than the real index (it would also block archived paths).']
    project_id [name: 'ix_features_project_id', note: 'proposed (scenario-service): feature list per project, including archived features (the partial unique index covers only active ones)']
  }
  Note: '''
  proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented.
  One Gherkin file. The Gherkin text in feature_versions is the source of truth. The rules, scenarios, steps, examples and example_rows tables are a parse of the current version only, kept for search, tag filtering and linking results (ERD-D3, ERD-D4).
  proposed (scenario-service): path uniqueness is case-insensitive and only among active features (partial unique index above). Concurrent writes in one project are serialised with a transaction-scoped PostgreSQL advisory lock keyed by project_id (there is no project row in this database).
  Living documentation = the current version of each non-archived feature plus the latest result per scenario. It is computed and needs no table in the MVP. Later: a doc_releases table (a named map of feature_id to version) for published snapshots.
  '''
}

Table feature_versions [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  version int [not null, note: 'starts at 1, +1 on every saved change']
  source text [not null, note: 'full Gherkin text of the file at this version. proposed (scenario-service): stored exactly as sent (line endings and trailing spaces kept), at most 1,000,000 code points, never containing U+0000 or a lone surrogate (spec D8).']
  content_hash varchar(64) [not null, note: 'SHA-256 hex of source; saving identical content creates no new version. proposed (scenario-service): hash of the UTF-8 bytes of source.']
  message varchar(500) [null, note: 'optional change message; blank is stored as null']
  created_by uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK)']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (feature_id, version) [unique]
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Immutable history of a feature. A diff between versions is computed from source, not stored. Later: import from Git (commit SHA per version) as a column. proposed (scenario-service): rows are never updated or deleted; a save is refused with VERSION_CONFLICT unless its base version equals features.current_version (spec D9).'
}

Table rules [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  keyword_text varchar(50) [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Rule (localised languages differ)']
  name text [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): text instead of varchar(500); may be empty']
  description text [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null, note: 'order among the children of the feature']
  line int [null, note: 'line number in the current version source']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. A Gherkin Rule (Gherkin 6+) that groups a Background and scenarios. proposed (scenario-service): rule ids are not stable across versions; clients must not keep them (spec D9).'
}

Table scenarios [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null, note: 'stable across versions when the scenario is matched on re-parse (ERD-D3); results reference it. proposed (scenario-service): matched by kind (BACKGROUND, SCENARIO, SCENARIO_OUTLINE), name and container (the feature, or a rule with the same name); with duplicate names the n-th old element matches the n-th new one (spec D9).']
  feature_id uuid [not null]
  rule_id uuid [null, note: 'set when the scenario or background sits inside a Rule']
  kind scenario_kind [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_scenarios_kind_values (ERD-D12)']
  keyword_text varchar(50) [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Scenario, Example, Scenario Outline, Background']
  name text [not null, note: 'a Background may have no name. proposed (scenario-service): text instead of varchar(1000); not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7).']
  description text [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null, note: 'order within the feature or rule']
  line int [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  Note: '''
  proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented.
  Holds Backgrounds, Scenarios and Scenario Outlines in one table so that steps have one parent. Rule enforced by the application: at most one BACKGROUND per feature and per rule.
  A **test case** is not stored: it is a SCENARIO, or one example row of a SCENARIO_OUTLINE (ERD-D5).
  '''
}

Table steps [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  scenario_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null]
  keyword step_keyword [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_steps_keyword_values (ERD-D12)']
  keyword_text varchar(50) [not null, note: 'keyword as written, e.g. Given, Soit (localised). proposed (scenario-service): without trailing whitespace.']
  step_text text [not null, note: 'step text without the keyword; may contain <placeholders> in outlines']
  argument_type step_argument_type [not null, default: 'NONE', note: 'proposed (scenario-service): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_steps_argument_type_values (ERD-D12). The application always sets it; the DBML default only documents the usual value.']
  data_table jsonb [null, note: 'when DATA_TABLE: array of rows, each an array of cell strings. proposed (scenario-service): jsonb instead of json.']
  doc_string text [null, note: 'when DOC_STRING: content between the delimiters']
  doc_string_media_type varchar(100) [null, note: 'optional media type after the opening delimiter, e.g. json']
  line int [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. A step has at most one argument: a data table or a doc string (ERD-D6). Later: a step definition library for autocomplete, kept in a table note until needed. proposed (scenario-service): step ids are not stable across versions; report_service.step_results relies on its text snapshot (spec D9).'
}

Table examples [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  scenario_id uuid [not null, note: 'must be a SCENARIO_OUTLINE (application rule)']
  keyword_text varchar(50) [not null, note: 'Examples or Scenarios, as written']
  name text [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): text instead of varchar(500); not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  description text [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): not null, empty string when absent (spec D19 #7)']
  position int [not null]
  header jsonb [not null, note: 'array of column names, e.g. ["user","result"]. proposed (scenario-service): jsonb instead of json; [] when the Examples block has no table (spec D19 #7).']
  line int [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. One Examples block of a Scenario Outline. Can carry its own tags. proposed (scenario-service): examples ids are not stable across versions (spec D9).'
}

Table example_rows [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null, note: 'referenced by results; one row = one test case. proposed (scenario-service): kept across versions when the outline keeps its id, the Examples block has the same header, and an old row has identical cells (each old row matches at most one new row, in order); a changed row gets a new id (spec D9).']
  examples_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null]
  cells jsonb [not null, note: 'array of cell strings, same length as examples.header. proposed (scenario-service): jsonb instead of json.']
  line int [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Kept as rows, not JSON inside examples, because each row is a test case that results point to.'
}

Table tags [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name text [not null, note: 'with the leading @, e.g. @smoke; compared case-sensitively like Cucumber tag expressions. proposed (scenario-service): text instead of varchar(255), so any tag the parser accepts can be stored (spec D8, D19 #5). One assignment per element even when the text repeats a tag (D19 #11).']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, name) [unique]
  }
  Note: '''
  proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Project-wide tag catalogue for filtering and autocomplete. Tags are written in the Gherkin text; this table is derived on parse (ERD-D7).
  proposed (scenario-service): the API lists only tags used in an active feature's current version, with the number of such features (featureCount). Whether a row with no assignment left is deleted or kept is an implementation choice (spec D12). Inserts run under the project advisory lock, so two saves introducing one new tag can't collide.
  '''
}

Table tag_assignments [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  tag_id uuid [not null]
  feature_id uuid [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): the feature whose current version carries the tag, whatever the target_type. Makes featureCount, the tag filter and clean-up on re-parse simple queries, and cascades with the feature.']
  target_type tag_target_type [not null, note: 'proposed (scenario-service): varchar(32) + CHECK ck_tag_assignments_target_type_values (ERD-D12)']
  target_id uuid [not null, note: 'id in features, rules, scenarios or examples depending on target_type. Polymorphic, so no FK; the parser keeps it consistent.']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (tag_id, target_type, target_id) [unique]
    (target_type, target_id)
    (feature_id, tag_id) [name: 'ix_tag_assignments_feature_id_tag_id', note: 'proposed (scenario-service): tag catalogue counts and the feature list tag filter; also indexes the feature_id foreign key']
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Which element carries which tag. Inherited tags (feature to scenario) are computed, not stored.'
}

Ref: feature_versions.feature_id > features.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (scenario-service): restrict, was cascade; versions are never deleted (spec D9, D14)
Ref: rules.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: scenarios.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: scenarios.rule_id > rules.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: steps.scenario_id > scenarios.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: examples.scenario_id > scenarios.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: example_rows.examples_id > examples.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: tag_assignments.tag_id > tags.id [delete: restrict] // proposed (scenario-service): restrict, was cascade; a catalogue row is only removed once unused (spec D12, D14)
Ref: tag_assignments.feature_id > features.id [delete: cascade] // proposed (scenario-service)

TableGroup scenario_service {
  features
  feature_versions
  rules
  scenarios
  steps
  examples
  example_rows
  tags
  tag_assignments
}

// =====================================================================
// PROPOSED: report-service (test runs and results) -- owner is decision ERD-D2
// =====================================================================

Enum execution_status {
  PASSED [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum). Cucumber statuses, stored upper case.']
  FAILED
  SKIPPED
  PENDING
  UNDEFINED
  AMBIGUOUS
  UNKNOWN [note: 'not executed yet, e.g. a planned manual test case. Same name as the Cucumber messages status (ERD-D8).']
}

Enum test_run_source {
  MANUAL [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum). Testers record results by hand.']
  AUTOMATED [note: 'results uploaded from a Cucumber run, e.g. by CI']
}

Enum test_run_status {
  PLANNED [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum)']
  IN_PROGRESS
  COMPLETED
  CANCELLED
}

Enum step_result_kind {
  STEP [note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented (whole enum)']
  BEFORE_HOOK
  AFTER_HOOK
}

Table environments [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(100) [not null, note: 'e.g. staging, production, Chrome 129']
  description text [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, name) [unique]
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Where a test run executed. Later: key/value attributes (browser, OS) as a json column.'
}

Table builds [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(255) [not null, note: 'build or version label, e.g. 1.4.2+517']
  branch varchar(255) [null]
  commit_sha varchar(64) [null]
  ci_url varchar(2048) [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, name) [unique]
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. The software build under test. Several runs (environments) can share one build.'
}

Table test_runs [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  project_id uuid [not null, note: 'references auth_service.projects.id (by ID, no FK)']
  name varchar(255) [not null]
  source test_run_source [not null]
  status test_run_status [not null, default: 'PLANNED']
  environment_id uuid [null]
  build_id uuid [null]
  tag_expression varchar(1000) [null, note: 'Cucumber tag expression that selected the scope, e.g. @smoke and not @wip']
  created_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); null when uploaded with a project token']
  started_at timestamptz [null]
  finished_at timestamptz [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (project_id, created_at)
  }
  Note: '''
  proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented.
  One execution of a set of test cases. MANUAL runs are created with one test_case_results row per selected test case in status UNKNOWN; AUTOMATED runs are created from an uploaded result file.
  Reports (pass rate, trends, per tag) are computed from runs and results; no report table in the MVP. Later: denormalised status counters on this table if queries get slow, and saved report filters.
  '''
}

Table test_case_results [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_run_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null, note: 'order in the run']
  feature_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.features.id (by ID, no FK); null when an uploaded result matches no known feature']
  feature_version_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.feature_versions.id (by ID, no FK); the version that was executed, if known']
  scenario_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.scenarios.id (by ID, no FK)']
  example_row_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.example_rows.id (by ID, no FK); set for Scenario Outline test cases']
  feature_path varchar(1024) [not null, note: 'snapshot at run time, so history survives edits and deletions']
  scenario_name varchar(1000) [not null, note: 'snapshot; for outlines, the name with placeholders filled in']
  tags json [null, note: 'snapshot: array of tag names incl. inherited ones']
  status execution_status [not null, default: 'UNKNOWN', note: 'worst step status using the Cucumber precedence; set by hand for MANUAL runs']
  attempt int [not null, default: 1, note: 'retry number for automated reruns']
  executed_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); the tester for MANUAL runs']
  comment text [null, note: 'tester remark for MANUAL runs']
  started_at timestamptz [null]
  finished_at timestamptz [null]
  duration_ms bigint [null]
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (test_run_id, position)
    scenario_id
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. The result of one test case (a scenario, or one example row of an outline) in one run.'
}

Table step_results [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_case_result_id uuid [not null]
  position int [not null, note: 'order of execution, including background steps and hooks']
  kind step_result_kind [not null, default: 'STEP']
  step_id uuid [null, note: 'references scenario_service.steps.id (by ID, no FK); null for hooks or unmatched steps']
  keyword_text varchar(50) [null, note: 'snapshot']
  step_text text [null, note: 'snapshot with outline placeholders filled in; null for hooks']
  status execution_status [not null, default: 'UNKNOWN']
  duration_ms bigint [null]
  error_message text [null, note: 'failure message and stack trace as reported by Cucumber']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    (test_case_result_id, position)
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Per-step status. Background steps appear here as ordinary steps of each test case, as in Cucumber output.'
}

Table attachments [headercolor: #D9822B] {
  id uuid [pk, not null]
  test_case_result_id uuid [not null]
  step_result_id uuid [null, note: 'set when attached to a step (screenshots, logs)']
  media_type varchar(255) [not null, note: 'e.g. image/png; logs use text/x.cucumber.log+plain']
  file_name varchar(255) [null]
  size_bytes bigint [not null]
  content bytea [not null, note: 'MVP: stored in the DB with a size cap (ERD-D9). Later: object storage with a storage_key column instead.']
  created_by uuid [null, note: 'references auth_service.users.id (by ID, no FK); null for automated uploads']
  created_at timestamptz [not null]

  indexes {
    test_case_result_id
  }
  Note: 'proposed — approved design (2026-10-12), not yet implemented. Screenshots, logs and other files attached to a test case or step result. Immutable.'
}

Ref: test_runs.environment_id > environments.id [delete: set null]
Ref: test_runs.build_id > builds.id [delete: set null]
Ref: test_case_results.test_run_id > test_runs.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: step_results.test_case_result_id > test_case_results.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: attachments.test_case_result_id > test_case_results.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: attachments.step_result_id > step_results.id [delete: cascade]

TableGroup report_service {
  environments
  builds
  test_runs
  test_case_results
  step_results
  attachments
}
